WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:01.750
- [Officer] Come back around on this side,

00:00:01.750 --> 00:00:03.350
and we'll send you in for the second test.

00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.200
- Thanks so much.

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:06.980
All right, here we go.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.668
Here goes nothing, but
even before I had that swab

00:00:09.668 --> 00:00:12.930
stuck basically into my
brain, I had a feeling

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.650
of what the result would be.

00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:16.170
- [Nurse] Felt like you
ate a little wasabi.

00:00:16.170 --> 00:00:17.770
- Yeah.

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:18.693
How did I know?

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:23.750
Because I turned my body
into a COVID-19 detecting

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.926
computer with various wearable devices.

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.843
(upbeat 80s music)

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:34.630
Yep, all these send data about my body

00:00:34.630 --> 00:00:36.883
via Bluetooth to apps on my iPhone.

00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:40.751
So why all the things?

00:00:40.751 --> 00:00:42.250
So why all the things?

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.730
Well, because medical
researchers and tech companies

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.790
have begun to see if
wearables can spot sickness,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.511
and right now, they're
very focused on COVID-19,

00:00:50.511 --> 00:00:52.433
and even seeing if these wearables

00:00:52.433 --> 00:00:54.734
can be an early detection system.

00:00:54.734 --> 00:00:57.495
Each of these continuously
monitors for one or more

00:00:57.495 --> 00:01:02.094
possible COVID-19 indicators,
higher body temperature,

00:01:02.094 --> 00:01:07.083
heart rate changes, low
blood oxygen levels.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.710
I'm going to take you
through each of these,

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:12.570
but before that, let me
be clear about something.

00:01:12.570 --> 00:01:16.640
None of these can tell you if
you do or don't have COVID.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.030
That's why I recruited Dr. Eric Topol,

00:01:19.030 --> 00:01:21.630
executive vice president
of Scripps Research.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.740
- Well, the problem is,

00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:25.870
is there's so much confounding potential

00:01:25.870 --> 00:01:30.870
of other things that could
cause a mild elevation

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:35.253
in temperature, a increase
in resting heart rate.

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:41.210
These parameters are
not that crisp a signal

00:01:41.730 --> 00:01:44.062
for COVID, only when they're together,

00:01:44.062 --> 00:01:46.178
and only when they were
in a cluster of people,

00:01:46.178 --> 00:01:48.500
do they become the real deal.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.013
- Still, I was committed to my experiment.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.130
I don't know if I'm going to
cough or throw up in my mask.

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.290
Number one, temperature tracking.

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:01.250
My average temp for the last
week, depends on what you ask.

00:02:01.250 --> 00:02:04.210
A fever is 100.4, according to the CDC.

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:07.450
The $300 Oura Ring was the
most interesting to me.

00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:10.170
It's one of the only wearables
that takes temperature,

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.540
and it doesn't give you a
readout of your core temperature,

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:14.010
like a regular thermometer.

00:02:14.010 --> 00:02:17.400
Instead, it figures out your
baseline temp over a few weeks,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.430
and then reports fluctuations.

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:20.910
The thing that's great about the Oura

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.680
is that it takes continuous temperature

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:24.050
in a comfortable way.

00:02:24.050 --> 00:02:25.970
A patch like this one from temp track

00:02:25.970 --> 00:02:27.810
does continuous core temperature,

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:29.900
but it's very uncomfortable,

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:31.730
and while I liked the
Kansas Smart Thermometer

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:33.900
the best, you have to remember to use it.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:36.070
What does all this
temperature data tell you?

00:02:36.070 --> 00:02:38.660
- Very little, unfortunately,

00:02:38.660 --> 00:02:42.660
The problem with temperature
is more than half of people

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:46.100
who have COVID-19, bonafide infection,

00:02:46.100 --> 00:02:48.670
they never mount a fever response,

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:49.790
and the other thing, of course,

00:02:49.790 --> 00:02:52.440
is that you're particularly infectious

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.180
before you have a fever,

00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:56.750
so what happens before you
have a temperature increase

00:02:56.750 --> 00:02:58.870
is your heart rate goes up many hours,

00:02:58.870 --> 00:03:02.670
or a day or two before,
so the heart rate resting

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.800
is actually more sensitive
than a temperature.

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.760
- Which brings me to number two,

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:09.763
heart rate and activity tracking.

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.136
My average resting heart
rate for the last week,

00:03:13.136 --> 00:03:16.530
according to Oura, 54 beats per minute.

00:03:16.530 --> 00:03:20.170
Garmin, Apple, and Fitbit
said 60 beats per minute.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:22.590
Oura says it only measures
heart rate at night,

00:03:22.590 --> 00:03:24.620
hence the lower average.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:29.330
- 30 To 40% of infections
of COVID are asymptomatic,

00:03:29.330 --> 00:03:31.850
no symptoms, but you should
be able to pick them up,

00:03:31.850 --> 00:03:34.190
if your heart rate, your
body is reacting to it,

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:35.430
even though you don't have symptoms,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.616
so the fact that your heart
rate has never gone up

00:03:37.616 --> 00:03:40.975
is a really good sign that
there's nothing going on,

00:03:40.975 --> 00:03:43.070
whether it's COVID or anything else.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.590
I mean, you're not even
under stress, even.

00:03:45.590 --> 00:03:49.160
- Okay, well, let's be clear,
I am under stress, okay, okay?

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.390
Researchers have started
to look at heart rate,

00:03:51.390 --> 00:03:53.770
respiratory activity, and sleep data

00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:56.540
in people who test positive for COVID-19.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.940
Once the studies and more
of the research is done,

00:03:58.940 --> 00:04:01.500
the idea is that these
wearables could get algorithms

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:05.140
that would look at our data
and give us some early warning.

00:04:05.140 --> 00:04:07.799
FitBit CEO James Park told
me that's the company's goal

00:04:07.799 --> 00:04:09.660
with its own study.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:14.370
- A user could receive a alert
that's color coded green,

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:17.350
yellow, red, and then they can assess

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.520
whether they need to self-quarantine

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:21.420
based on that risk assessment,

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:23.850
and then follow up with a physician

00:04:23.850 --> 00:04:26.013
for a traditional nasal swab test.

00:04:26.013 --> 00:04:28.660
- Oura already doing
something similar with the NBA

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.270
in the Orlando Bubble.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:33.793
Wearers are notified if data
points hit certain levels.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:40.220
Number three, blood oxygen tracking.

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:42.160
My average blood oxygen level this week

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:45.320
from a Walgreen's pulse oximeter, 98%,

00:04:45.320 --> 00:04:47.760
the Garmin 96%,

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:50.250
A low blood oxygen level,
something in the 80

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:54.220
or low 90% range can be
a signal for COVID-19,

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.530
which has made pulse
oximeters the hottest gadget

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:58.670
of the year, but if you
have one of Garmin's

00:04:58.670 --> 00:05:01.070
latest wearables, you
don't need to buy one.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:02.600
It's built right in.

00:05:02.600 --> 00:05:04.660
Dr. Topol said my scores looked good,

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:05.830
but that with blood oxygen,

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:09.250
it's only helpful for people
already diagnosed with COVID-19

00:05:09.250 --> 00:05:11.840
to gauge the severity of the illness.

00:05:11.840 --> 00:05:12.945
There's one last thing our wearables

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:16.120
might end up with, cough monitoring.

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:18.710
This patch from Northwestern
being used in studies

00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:22.020
tracked my coughs, even my throat clears.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:24.453
According to the readouts, I was all good,

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:30.340
and then, it was finally
time to ask, do I have COVID?

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:32.023
- No, you don't have COVID.

00:05:32.023 --> 00:05:34.796
I'll rest my case, you don't have covert.

00:05:34.796 --> 00:05:37.660
Of course, you have to
have a test to prove that.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.493
- A few days later,

00:05:38.493 --> 00:05:40.970
my official test results
said the same thing,

00:05:40.970 --> 00:05:43.068
and maybe the best thing
about this wearable data

00:05:43.068 --> 00:05:45.800
is telling you if you
should get a test or not.

00:05:45.800 --> 00:05:49.070
- So the way I look at it
is, in the months ahead,

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:52.670
people will have at
their home a testing kit

00:05:52.670 --> 00:05:55.420
that will give them the
answer in 15 minutes,

00:05:55.420 --> 00:05:58.820
and they'll also be using
wearables, if they're smart,

00:05:58.820 --> 00:06:01.479
because they already have
these devices largely,

00:06:01.479 --> 00:06:03.610
and so, you wouldn't do the test unless

00:06:03.610 --> 00:06:05.659
either you had symptoms or your sensors

00:06:05.659 --> 00:06:09.670
were coming together, that
there's something going on.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:11.760
- The one problem with that is
that some of the communities

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:14.990
hit hardest by COVID-19 may
not have access to these

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.960
sometimes pricey wearables,

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:19.840
but at least you don't need to own or wear

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:21.253
all the things at once.

